---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { atlas } from "../../lib/atlas";
import { COMMUNITY_STATUSES, communityBlurb, communityLabel, communityLabelFor } from "../../lib/lenses";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const changed = atlas.families.filter(
  (family) => (family.community?.status ?? "claimed") !== "claimed",
);
---

<Base
  title="Community status · Math Release Atlas"
  description="The community-status vocabulary, the evidence rule, and which families are not claimed."
>
  <article class="prose status-page">
    <h1>Community status</h1>
    <p>
      A family stays claimed until a pull request changes it. Every status change must be
      approved by Jason (repo policy). The weekly sync does not choose a status.
    </p>

    <h2>Vocabulary</h2>
    <ul class="status-list">
      {
        COMMUNITY_STATUSES.map((status) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{communityLabel(status)}</strong>
            <span class="meta"> {status}</span>
            <p>{communityBlurb(status)}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <h2>Evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Any status other than claimed needs an http or https URL, a date in YYYY-MM-DD form, and a
      short neutral note of at most 25 words. A history entry whose status is not claimed needs
      the same three fields. A claimed entry may omit them.
    </p>

    <h2>How a status changes</h2>
    <p>
      Edit the family file under <code>data/curated/</code> and open a pull request. The vocabulary
      file is <code>data/curated/community-status.yaml</code>. Steps for that pull request are in
      <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code>. The weekly sync copies generated catalogue files only. It does
      not edit curated notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      A status other than claimed passes Guard only when
      <code>data/curated/status-approvals.yaml</code> has a matching entry. The entry lists the
      family id, the status, the evidence URL, the date, the note, and the approver jkbennitt.
      Editing the note or the date after that entry is written fails Guard. The allowlist starts
      empty. <code>CODEOWNERS</code> names @jkbennitt on <code>data/curated/</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Families that are not claimed</h2>
    {
      changed.length === 0 ? (
        <p>Every family in this catalogue is claimed.</p>
      ) : (
        <ul class="status-list">
          {changed.map((family) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`${base}f/${family.id}/`}>{family.id}</a>
              <span class="meta"> · {communityLabelFor(family.community?.status)}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )
    }
  </article>
</Base>
